"on-premise","premise indicator","major premise","minor premise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4a07019922ba7d0b53","definition":"To set forth beforehand, or as introductory to the main subject; to offer previously, as something to explain or aid in understanding what follows.","example":"I premise these particulars that the reader may know that I enter upon it as a very ungrateful task.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["counterpremise","off-premise","on-premise","premise indicator","major premise","minor premise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8d98333a5ecdd0da22","definition":"To send before the time, or beforehand; hence, to cause to be before something else; to employ previously.","example":"the premised flames of the last day","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["counterpremise","off-premise","on-premise","premise indicator","major premise","minor premise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/premise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈpɹɛm.ɪs/"},"wordFamily":["counterpremise","off-premise","on-premise","premise indicator","major premise","minor premise"]}